\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For the source-defined even-circumference honeycomb cylinder loop partition $Z_N(chi)$ with separating-loop fugacity $chi>0$, is $Z_N(chi)=N^(\tau (chi)+o(1))$, where $\tau =1/6-2(arccos(chi/2))^2/(3\pi ^2)$ for $0<chi\leq 2$ and $\tau =1/6+2(arcosh(chi/2))^2/(3\pi ^2)$ for $chi\geq 2$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For the source-defined even-circumference honeycomb cylinder loop partition $Z_N(chi)$ with separating-loop fugacity $chi>0$, is $Z_N(chi)=N^(\tau (chi)+o(1))$, where $\tau =1/6-2(arccos(chi/2))^2/(3\pi ^2)$ for $0<chi\leq 2$ and $\tau =1/6+2(arcosh(chi/2))^2/(3\pi ^2)$ for $chi\geq 2$?

